' ============================================================================
' 51 Rules set at a time (TL-2b): one snapshot, one eval, the derived facts.
'
' Source of Figure TL17 in ../tensor-logic/integration.md (section 4). The
' figure restates TL-2b of that section and the example of
' tensor-logic/syntax.md section 4.17. It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. The deploy reads one snapshot of a relation: a peek of a cell, or a
'      list read of a VectorDB collection of facts.
'   2. It calls eval with a tl:Program of rules, and the snapshot as one
'      tensor in the value ABI (form V2).
'   3. The TL engine checks safety and stratification, then runs the
'      semi-naive iteration until no new fact appears.
'   4. The reply holds the derived facts of the queries, which the deploy
'      can send to a space.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 51-tl-set-at-a-time.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 51-tl-set-at-a-time
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor $rrs_relation
  LifeLineBorderColor $rrs_relation
  ParticipantBorderColor $rrs_relation
  ActorBorderColor $rrs_relation
  GroupBorderColor $rrs_relation
  DividerBorderColor $rrs_relation
  DividerBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
}
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title Rules set at a time: TL-2b (integration 4)
autonumber

participant "Deploy" as DEPLOY $rrs_host
database "RSpace\n(the cell kb)" as RSPACE $rrs_storage
participant "rho:lang:vector\n[0xE0, 0x23]" as VEC $rrs_system
participant "TL engine" as ENGINE $rrs_tl_engine

DEPLOY -> RSPACE : for (@kb <<- @"kb") { ... }
RSPACE --> DEPLOY : one snapshot of the relation:\nSet(("Alice", "Bob"), ("Bob", "Charlie"))
DEPLOY -> VEC : vec!?("eval", tl:Program{\n  Ancestor(x, y) <- Parent(x, y) |\n  Ancestor(x, z) <- Ancestor(x, y), Parent(y, z) |\n  Ancestor("Alice", x)? }, {"Parent": kb}, {})
VEC -> ENGINE : the program and the relation (form V2)
ENGINE -> ENGINE : CHECK: every rule is safe, and negation is stratified
ENGINE -> ENGINE : <latex>R \leftarrow \Delta \leftarrow</latex> the facts and the non-recursive rules
loop while <latex>\Delta \neq \emptyset</latex> (reserving each join first)
  ENGINE -> ENGINE : <latex>N \leftarrow</latex> the rules with an atom from <latex>\Delta</latex>
  ENGINE -> ENGINE : <latex>\Delta \leftarrow N \setminus R,\ R \leftarrow R \cup \Delta</latex>
end
ENGINE --> VEC : Ancestor("Alice", x): x = "Bob" and x = "Charlie"
VEC --> DEPLOY : [true, {the query: Set("Bob", "Charlie")}]\n(the slice, in the value ABI)
opt keep the derived facts
  DEPLOY -> RSPACE : send each derived fact to a space
end
note over RSPACE, VEC
  A list-mode bind cannot sit in a join (ListModeInJoin),
  so one deploy reads one snapshot (open question K9).
end note

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_host>      | the deploy |
|<$rrs_storage>   | consensus state in RSpace |
|<$rrs_system>    | the capability |
|<$rrs_tl_engine> | the TL engine |
endlegend
@enduml
